1.0.4-snapshot
  The FurnitureFuel name, the modded exes check and a lamp timer fix
    Hideout Furniture Infinite Fuel is now FurnitureFuel, and it writes a separate furniturefuel.log.
    The load check now stops the game with a message when the modded exes are missing or too old, and when xlibs is older than 1.5.1.
    Other things you will notice. The lamp timer works in modpacks that replace the vanilla timer queue, and the log names the mod, xlibs and exe versions.

  - Changed the mod name to FurnitureFuel. It logs to a separate furniturefuel.log.
  - Added the modded exes check. The game stops at load with a message when it finds neither demonized 20250908 or newer nor AOEngine.
  - Changed the xlibs requirement to 1.5.1.
  - Added the mod, xlibs and exe versions to the log at startup.
  - Fixed the lamp switch-off timer in modpacks that replace the vanilla timer queue, such as demonized time events.

1.0.3
  An xlibs 1.2.3 floor, with newer xlibs accepted
    From this release the load check accepts xlibs 1.2.3 or any newer compatible version, where it used to ask for 1.2.1 exactly.

  - Changed the xlibs check to accept 1.2.3 or any newer compatible version. It used to stop the game on any version but 1.2.1.

1.0.2
  The xlibs 1.2.1 requirement
    This release runs on xlibs 1.2.1, and the load check asks for that exact version.

  - Changed the xlibs requirement to 1.2.1.

1.0.1
  The xlibs dependency check
    The mod now needs xlibs and checks its version at load.

  - Added the xlibs requirement, with a check at load that stops the game with a message when xlibs is missing or outdated.

1.0.0
  Infinite fuel for placeable lights
    In the first release the metal torch, the gas lamp and the light altar burn without batteries, kerosene or gauss ammo.

  - Added infinite fuel for every placeable light. Flicker, sounds and the on and off switch work as before.
